+# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
+# [MP8] Train Race (train_race, mp8game=9) 8-player adaptation — ① adaptation (2026-08-17)
+# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
+#
+# ### Diagnostic findings (measured from the stock PCK with probe53/54, not guessed)
+#
+# **Good news - this minigame's core gameplay already scales with player count, not a single character needs changing.**
+# nook_handler.gd:30 `nooks_to_open = max((player_count + 2) - rounds_passed, 1)`,
+# and `player_count` is refreshed every round by train_race.gd from `active_players.size()` (see _on_cycle_finished).
+# How many open is computed, and the loop upper bound is `nooks.size()`, **not indexed by player index → never out of bounds**.
+#
+# Ran the pitfall #13 grep across the whole directory. **Only one place indexes by player index** — the spawn_players() below,
+# at `player_spawn_positions[counter]`. 4 points and 8 players, so from counter=4 onward it is guaranteed to go out of bounds.
+#
+# ### ⚠️⚠️ Why this minigame must manage its own spawn points (pitfall #33, worse here than in DVD Roomba)
+#
+# The **scene order of the 4 vanilla Markers is diagonally crossed again** (world coordinates measured by probe53).
+#     [0]=(-3.95,-4.06)  [1]=(3.42,4.19)  [2]=(-3.97,4.55)  [3]=(4.11,-4.00)
+# Container-style top-up (network_manager `_mp8_topup`) takes "the midpoint of two adjacent points", and here "adjacent" picks the diagonals.
+#     j=0: mid([0],[1]) = (-0.27, 0.07)
+#     j=2: mid([2],[3]) = ( 0.07, 0.28)   ← only **0.40 m from j=0, basically on top of each other**
+# And both points land at **x≈0**, which is **the center line the train runs over**.
+# → `mp8_owns_spawns = true` is required so the generic top-up steps aside.
+#
+# ⚠️ The container name `PlayerSpawnPositions` is **shared with Disco Dodge**,
+# so it must never be removed from `MP8_SPAWN_CONTAINERS` the way Duck Hunt / Manufacture Gun were — that would break the already signed-off Disco Dodge.
+# Take the `mp8_owns_spawns` route instead, which only affects this minigame.
+#
+# ### Placement for this minigame - **evenly spaced inserts per column** (no hard-coded coordinates, computed live from the vanilla points)
+#
+# The 4 vanilla points are really 2 columns × 2 rows. Left column x≈-3.96, right column x≈+3.4~4.1, and z is about ±4 in each.
+# Approach - split into two columns by the sign of x, then insert 2 evenly spaced points in each column **between its own two endpoints** (lerping x as well).
+# So every new point is **a convex combination of two vanilla points in the same column**, and naturally lands inside the vanilla convex hull (a hard constraint set in T4b),
+# and **none of them lands on the x≈0 center line**.
+#   Left column z span 8.61 → spacing 2.87 m, right column z span 8.19 → spacing 2.73 m
+#   Minimum spacing **2.73 m** (vs 0.40 m with the generic top-up)
+# The 4 vanilla points don't change by a single byte — 4-player matches match vanilla value for value.
+var mp8_owns_spawns: bool = true
+
+# Required minimum gap between a new point and any existing point. Below it we log a warning (report only, no blocking, so problems surface if placement is changed later)
+const MP8_MIN_SPAWN_GAP: float = 1.5
+const MP8_MAX_PLAYERS: int = 8
+
+var mp8_player_count: int = 0
+
